  "user_impact": "Screen readers do not announce status messages correctly.",
  "technical_impact": "Conflict between role (alert/status/log/timer) and aria-live value.",
  "source": "WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 Status Messages; WAI-ARIA 1.2 alert, status, log (implicit aria-live) and aria-live",
  "applicability": "Elements in the accessibility tree with role alert, status or log (explicit or implicit, <output> is status) and an aria-live attribute.",
  "expectation": "Fails for aria-live=\"off\": updates of the status message are not announced. Changing the\nurgency (alert with polite, status with assertive) is allowed by ARIA and still announced: review.\nThe default urgency, stated or implicit, passes; a log may change its urgency; aria-live on an\nelement without a live role is not this id. Hidden subtrees are out of scope.",
  "method": "shared",
